    "description": {
      "value": "<p><em>Wondrous Item, Artifact (Requires Attunement)</em></p><p>A wizard named Damara made this orb while seeking a way to become a dragon. With the help of a mysterious magician—in truth an aspect of Tiamat in disguise—Damara at last created an Artifact that would fulfill his dream. Yet its power frightened him so much that he dared not use it; instead, he sealed himself in a tomb with the orb to lock it away.</p><p>The orb is about 6 inches across and made of a glassy, iridescent material like obsidian, but incredibly hard. If someone holds it to their lips intending to swallow it, the orb shrinks to the size of a grape.</p><p><strong>Properties of the Orb.</strong> While attuned to the orb, you gain the following benefits.</p><p><strong>Dragon’s Breath.</strong> You can take a Magic action to exhale a 15-foot Cone of Acid, Cold, Fire, Lightning, or Poison (your choice). Each creature in the Cone makes a DC 18 Dexterity saving throw, taking 6d6 damage of the chosen type on a failed save or half as much damage on a successful one.</p><p><strong>Fear Aura.</strong> While you don’t have the &amp;Reference[Incapacitated apply=false] condition, you radiate a terrifying aura in a 20-foot Emanation, which you can turn off or on as a Magic action. Any enemy that starts its turn in the aura must succeed on a DC 18 Wisdom saving throw or have the &amp;Reference[Frightened apply=false] condition until the start of its next turn. A creature that succeeds on this save is immune to the aura for 24 hours.</p><p><strong>Flight.</strong> You have a Fly Speed of 60 feet and can hover.</p><p><strong>Random Properties.</strong> The Artifact has the following random properties (see chapter 7 of the <em>Dungeon Master’s Guide</em>):</p><ul><li><p>2 minor beneficial properties</p></li><li><p>2 minor detrimental properties</p></li></ul><p><strong>Spellcasting.</strong> The orb has 6 charges and regains 1d4 + 2 expended charges daily at dawn. While attuned to it, you can cast one of the spells on the following table from it (+10 spell attack modifier, spell save DC 18), expending the number of charges it shows.</p><table><thead><tr><th>Spell</th><th>Charge Cost</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>@UUID[Compendium.dnd5e.spells24.Item.phbsplDisguiseSe]{Disguise Self}</td><td>0</td></tr><tr><td>@UUID[Compendium.dnd5e.spells24.Item.phbsplFireShield]{Fire Shield}</td><td>2</td></tr><tr><td>@UUID[Compendium.dnd5e.spells24.Item.phbsplHoldPerson]{Hold Person}</td><td>1</td></tr><tr><td>@UUID[Compendium.dnd5e.spells24.Item.phbsplSeeInvisib]{See Invisibility}</td><td>1</td></tr><tr><td>@UUID[Compendium.dnd5e.spells24.Item.phbsplSummonDrag]{Summon Dragon} (level 9 version)</td><td>4</td></tr></tbody></table><p><strong>Dragon Transformation.</strong> If you swallow the orb, you transform into an adult chromatic dragon under the DM’s control; the DM chooses its kind according to your alignment and personality. The transformation is permanent, but if the dragon is slain, its body returns to its original form and the orb reappears outside it.</p><p><strong>Destroying the Orb.</strong> If an @UUID[Compendium.dnd5e.actors24.Actor.mmAncientGoldDra]{Ancient Gold Dragon} willingly swallows the orb, both the orb and the dragon are destroyed.</p><section class=\"secret\" id=\"secret-NFgGDsO7Ty7vhpgZ\"><p><strong>Foundry Note</strong></p><p>Les propriétés aléatoires d’artefact sont à ajouter par le MJ.</p></section>",
      "chat": ""
    },
